{
  "title": "Numbers and Strings",
  "summary": "Floating point, NaN, conversion, template literals and string methods.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "One number type",
      "body": [
        "Every `number` is a 64-bit floating-point value, like C# `double`. That has consequences:",
        "",
        "```ts",
        "console.log(7 / 2);          // 3.5   (no integer division)",
        "console.log(Math.floor(7 / 2)); // 3",
        "console.log(0.1 + 0.2);      // 0.30000000000000004",
        "console.log(1 / 0);          // Infinity  (no exception)",
        "```",
        "",
        "For money, store whole cents (`1999`, not `19.99`) and format at the end.",
        "",
        "`%` is remainder, `**` is power: `2 ** 10` is `1024`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "console.log(10 / 4);",
        "console.log(Math.trunc(10 / 4), 10 % 4);",
        "console.log(2 ** 3);"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "2.5",
        "2 2",
        "8"
      ],
      "explain": "`/` always gives a floating-point result. `Math.trunc` drops the fraction, `%` is the remainder, `**` raises to a power."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "NaN and conversion",
      "body": [
        "`NaN` (\"not a number\") is what failed arithmetic produces. It does not throw:",
        "",
        "```ts",
        "console.log(Number(\"42\"));     // 42",
        "console.log(Number(\"42px\"));   // NaN",
        "console.log(parseInt(\"42px\")); // 42  (reads leading digits)",
        "console.log(Number(\"\"));       // 0   (careful!)",
        "```",
        "",
        "`NaN === NaN` is `false`, so test with `Number.isNaN(x)`. Format with `toFixed`, which returns a **string**:",
        "",
        "```ts",
        "console.log((2.5).toFixed(2));   // \"2.50\"",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "match",
      "prompt": "Match each expression to its result.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "`Number(\"7\")`",
          "`7`"
        ],
        [
          "`Number(\"7a\")`",
          "`NaN`"
        ],
        [
          "`parseInt(\"7a\")`",
          "`7` (leading digits)"
        ],
        [
          "`(7).toFixed(1)`",
          "`\"7.0\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`Number(\"\")`",
          "`0`"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Template literals and string methods",
      "body": [
        "Backtick strings are **template literals**, JavaScript's `$\"...\"` interpolation:",
        "",
        "```ts",
        "const item = \"tea\", qty = 3;",
        "console.log(`${qty} x ${item}`);      // 3 x tea",
        "console.log(`total: ${qty * 2.5}`);   // total: 7.5",
        "```",
        "",
        "They can also span several lines. Useful string members (strings are immutable, as in C#):",
        "",
        "| JavaScript | C# |",
        "|---|---|",
        "| `s.length` | `s.Length` |",
        "| `s.toUpperCase()` | `s.ToUpper()` |",
        "| `s.trim()` | `s.Trim()` |",
        "| `s.includes(\"x\")` | `s.Contains(\"x\")` |",
        "| `s.startsWith(\"x\")` | `s.StartsWith(\"x\")` |",
        "| `s.slice(1, 3)` | `s[1..3]` |",
        "| `s.split(\",\")` | `s.Split(',')` |",
        "| `s.padStart(5, \"0\")` | `s.PadLeft(5, '0')` |",
        "| `s.replaceAll(\"a\", \"b\")` | `s.Replace(\"a\", \"b\")` |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "const word = \"  Dojo  \";",
        "const t = word.trim();",
        "console.log(`[${t}] ${t.length}`);",
        "console.log(t.slice(1).toUpperCase());"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "[Dojo] 4",
        "OJO"
      ],
      "explain": "`trim` removes the outer spaces. `slice(1)` takes from index 1 to the end."
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Complete the code so it prints `Order 007: 3 items`.",
      "code": [
        "const id = 7, count = 3;",
        "console.log(__1__Order ${String(id).__2__(3, \"0\")}: ${__3__} items__1__);"
      ],
      "blanks": [
        "`",
        "padStart",
        "count"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "\"",
        "padEnd",
        "id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Price label",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `priceLabel(name: string, cents: number): string`.",
        "",
        "It returns the name, a colon, a space, a dollar sign and the price with exactly two decimals:",
        "",
        "- `priceLabel(\"Tea\", 250)` returns `\"Tea: $2.50\"`",
        "- `priceLabel(\"Cake\", 1999)` returns `\"Cake: $19.99\"`",
        "",
        "Use a template literal."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "function priceLabel(name: string, cents: number): string {",
        "  return \"\";",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "function priceLabel(name: string, cents: number): string {",
        "  return `${name}: $${(cents / 100).toFixed(2)}`;",
        "}"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "Dojo.eq('priceLabel(\"Tea\", 250)', \"Tea: $2.50\", priceLabel(\"Tea\", 250));",
        "Dojo.eq('priceLabel(\"Cake\", 1999)', \"Cake: $19.99\", priceLabel(\"Cake\", 1999));",
        "Dojo.eq('priceLabel(\"Gum\", 5)', \"Gum: $0.05\", priceLabel(\"Gum\", 5));"
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "`",
          "message": "Uses a template literal"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Divide by 100 to get dollars, then `.toFixed(2)`.",
        "A literal `$` followed by `${...}` is written `$${...}`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Parse a quantity",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `parseQty(text: string): number` for a form field:",
        "",
        "- trim spaces, then convert with `Number`",
        "- return the number if it is a whole number of at least 1 (use `Number.isInteger`)",
        "- otherwise return `0` (this covers `\"\"`, `\"abc\"`, `\"2.5\"`, `\"-3\"`)",
        "",
        "`parseQty(\" 4 \")` is `4`."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "function parseQty(text: string): number {",
        "  return 0;",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "function parseQty(text: string): number {",
        "  const t = text.trim();",
        "  if (t === \"\") return 0;",
        "  const n = Number(t);",
        "  return Number.isInteger(n) && n >= 1 ? n : 0;",
        "}"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "Dojo.eq('parseQty(\" 4 \")', 4, parseQty(\" 4 \"));",
        "Dojo.eq('parseQty(\"12\")', 12, parseQty(\"12\"));",
        "Dojo.eq('parseQty(\"\")', 0, parseQty(\"\"));",
        "Dojo.eq('parseQty(\"   \")', 0, parseQty(\"   \"));",
        "Dojo.eq('parseQty(\"abc\")', 0, parseQty(\"abc\"));",
        "Dojo.eq('parseQty(\"2.5\")', 0, parseQty(\"2.5\"));",
        "Dojo.eq('parseQty(\"-3\")', 0, parseQty(\"-3\"));"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`Number(\"\")` is `0`, and `Number(\"abc\")` is `NaN`. `Number.isInteger(NaN)` is false.",
        "Return `n` only when `Number.isInteger(n) && n >= 1`."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
